WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Welcome. This class begins before
downloading or running a model.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
You will identify the exact deployment
object, separate public access

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
from legal permission and Open Source
claims, review all applicable

4
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
terms against an intended use, trace model
lineage without filling

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
gaps with assumptions, and issue a dated
decision with clear

6
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.000
reviewer authority. A model family
nickname can help you search.

7
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.000
It cannot prove which bytes, terms,
transformations, or runtime you

8
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.000
intend to operate.

9
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Start by naming the object under review.
Separate the complete

10
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:52.000
AI system from the model architecture,
weight files, tokenizer, configuration,

11
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:58.000
prompt or chat template, adapters,
quantization, inference runtime,

12
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:04.000
dependencies, and surrounding application.
Each component can come from a

13
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:10.000
different publisher, carry a different
version or license, and introduce

14
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:16.000
a different security or failure boundary.
Record a deployment tuple:

15
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:22.000
publisher and repository, immutable
revision, filenames and cryptographic

16
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:28.000
digests, base-model lineage, derivative or
adapter identity, quantization method and

17
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:34.000
parameters, tokenizer, template, runtime
and version, and intended deployment

18
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.000
shape. Use immutable identifiers, not a
mutable branch, latest alias,

19
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:46.000
cache name, or friendly label. If a
material field is

20
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:52.000
unknown, mark it unresolved. Do not
quietly replace the missing

21
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:58.000
value with the most likely answer. The
tuple is the

22
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:04.000
target for legal review, integrity
verification, compatibility tests,

23
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:10.000
evaluation, deployment, and later incident
response.

24
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.455
Imagine a repository described only as a
seven-billion-parameter assistant. The

25
00:02:15.455 --> 00:02:20.909
proposed file is a four-bit quantization
uploaded by a community

26
00:02:20.909 --> 00:02:26.364
publisher. Its card links to a fine-tune,
which links to

27
00:02:26.364 --> 00:02:31.818
a base model. The runtime applies a
separate chat template.

28
00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:37.273
The name alone hides four publishers,
three transformations, several sets

29
00:02:37.273 --> 00:02:42.727
of terms, and the runtime contract. A
defensible record pins

30
00:02:42.727 --> 00:02:48.182
each link, file, digest, quantization
setting, tokenizer, template, and runtime.

31
00:02:48.182 --> 00:02:53.636
If the base revision or conversion recipe
cannot be found,

32
00:02:53.636 --> 00:02:59.091
the lineage is incomplete. That does not
automatically prove danger,

33
00:02:59.091 --> 00:03:04.545
but it prevents a confident identity claim
and changes the

34
00:03:04.545 --> 00:03:10.000
allowed decision.

35
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:16.071
Next, use precise labels. Publicly
downloadable weights establish that

36
00:03:16.071 --> 00:03:22.143
someone can obtain the files under
presented conditions. They do

37
00:03:22.143 --> 00:03:28.214
not establish commercial permission,
modification rights, redistribution

38
00:03:28.214 --> 00:03:34.286
rights, safety, provenance, support, or
source transparency. Open-weight is

39
00:03:34.286 --> 00:03:40.357
commonly used for accessible weights, but
the exact terms may

40
00:03:40.357 --> 00:03:46.429
restrict fields of use, users, scale,
outputs, modification, or distribution.

41
00:03:46.429 --> 00:03:52.500
The Open Source Initiative's Open Source
AI Definition version one

42
00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:58.571
evaluates freedoms to use, study, modify,
and share, together with

43
00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:04.643
access to the preferred form for
modification. When you make

44
00:04:04.643 --> 00:04:10.714
an Open Source AI claim, cite the exact
definition and

45
00:04:10.714 --> 00:04:16.786
evidence. When the evidence only shows
downloadable weights under named

46
00:04:16.786 --> 00:04:22.857
terms, say exactly that. Precise language
is not a branding

47
00:04:22.857 --> 00:04:28.929
debate. It prevents technical teams,
learners, downstream users, and

48
00:04:28.929 --> 00:04:35.000
distributors from receiving permissions
that the evidence never granted.

49
00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:41.250
Checkpoint. The weights can be downloaded,
but the repository links

50
00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:47.500
to additional terms and the right to
redistribute a quantized

51
00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:53.750
derivative is unclear. Which claim can you
safely make now,

52
00:04:53.750 --> 00:05:00.000
and which claim must wait for evidence or
authorized interpretation?

53
00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:20.714
A strong answer says only that the weights
are publicly

54
00:06:20.714 --> 00:06:26.429
obtainable under the presented conditions.
Redistribution of the derivative is

55
00:06:26.429 --> 00:06:32.143
not established until the controlling
terms and lineage are reviewed.

56
00:06:32.143 --> 00:06:37.857
The complete system should not be called
Open Source AI

57
00:06:37.857 --> 00:06:43.571
merely because one set of weights is
downloadable. If your

58
00:06:43.571 --> 00:06:49.286
answer treated access as permission,
revise it by naming the

59
00:06:49.286 --> 00:06:55.000
exact right you need and the evidence that
grants it.

60
00:06:55.000 --> 00:07:01.786
Review the applicable terms as one system.
Collect the license

61
00:07:01.786 --> 00:07:08.571
text from the pinned revision, repository
terms, acceptable-use policy, model

62
00:07:08.571 --> 00:07:15.357
card, notices, attribution requirements,
base-model terms, adapter or dataset

63
00:07:15.357 --> 00:07:22.143
obligations, and deployment or
distribution conditions. Record the

64
00:07:22.143 --> 00:07:28.929
retrieved version and date. A short
license metadata field helps

65
00:07:28.929 --> 00:07:35.714
discovery but does not replace controlling
text. Map the intended

66
00:07:35.714 --> 00:07:42.500
use across internal or external access,
commercial use, modification, fine-tuning,

67
00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:49.286
generated-output terms, hosting an API,
redistribution, derivative sharing,

68
00:07:49.286 --> 00:07:56.071
attribution, notice preservation,
downstream restrictions, geography, scale,

69
00:07:56.071 --> 00:08:02.857
users, and termination. Separate facts
from interpretations. Educational content

70
00:08:02.857 --> 00:08:09.643
and model output can organize evidence;
they cannot issue legal

71
00:08:09.643 --> 00:08:16.429
approval. Send ambiguity that changes a
consequential decision to an

72
00:08:16.429 --> 00:08:23.214
authorized legal or policy reviewer with
the exact sources, artifact

73
00:08:23.214 --> 00:08:30.000
tuple, and intended use.

74
00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:36.923
Trace lineage through every material
transformation. A model card may

75
00:08:36.923 --> 00:08:43.846
describe intended uses, limits, datasets,
training, evaluations, base models,

76
00:08:43.846 --> 00:08:50.769
licenses, and library compatibility. Treat
each field as a claim

77
00:08:50.769 --> 00:08:57.692
to verify. Follow the base model,
fine-tune, adapter, merge, conversion,

78
00:08:57.692 --> 00:09:04.615
and quantization references until the
proposed artifact's ancestry is

79
00:09:04.615 --> 00:09:11.538
understood. Label each statement directly
evidenced, inferred, unknown, or requiring

80
00:09:11.538 --> 00:09:18.462
authorized interpretation. Record missing
training information, unclear derivative

81
00:09:18.462 --> 00:09:25.385
relationships, absent evaluations,
conflicting terms, unverified publishers,

82
00:09:25.385 --> 00:09:32.308
and incompatible versions. Never ask a
model to invent a

83
00:09:32.308 --> 00:09:39.231
plausible bridge between two missing
records. Choose an explicit response:

84
00:09:39.231 --> 00:09:46.154
stop, request evidence, select another
artifact, or permit only a

85
00:09:46.154 --> 00:09:53.077
bounded isolated evaluation through the
authorized process. The gap remains

86
00:09:53.077 --> 00:10:00.000
visible even when a reviewer accepts
residual risk.

87
00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:06.667
Finish with a dated, scoped, and expiring
adoption decision. Include

88
00:10:06.667 --> 00:10:13.333
the exact artifact tuple, intended and
prohibited uses, applicable terms,

89
00:10:13.333 --> 00:10:20.000
required notices, lineage, authoritative
sources, gaps, reviewers, approval scope,

90
00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:26.667
decision date, and expiry or re-review
triggers. Keep technical recommendation,

91
00:10:26.667 --> 00:10:33.333
security review, legal or policy
interpretation, and operational acceptance

92
00:10:33.333 --> 00:10:40.000
as distinct authorities. One signature
should not be misread as

93
00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:46.667
every kind of approval. Re-review when the
publisher, revision, license,

94
00:10:46.667 --> 00:10:53.333
use policy, base model, adapter,
quantization, tokenizer, template,

95
00:10:53.333 --> 00:11:00.000
runtime, deployment audience, distribution
method, or use case changes. Preserve

96
00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:06.667
rejected candidates and reasons. This
record lets a later operator

97
00:11:06.667 --> 00:11:13.333
explain not only what runs, but why it was

98
00:11:13.333 --> 00:11:20.000
selected and when that decision must be
challenged.

99
00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:26.429
Now build the identity and terms decision
using a low-risk

100
00:11:26.429 --> 00:11:32.857
candidate repository without downloading
or executing its files. Complete the

101
00:11:32.857 --> 00:11:39.286
immutable tuple, retrieve exact terms, map
proposed uses, trace lineage,

102
00:11:39.286 --> 00:11:45.714
label every claim by evidence status, and
choose approve for

103
00:11:45.714 --> 00:11:52.143
isolated evaluation, reject, or hold for
evidence. Include reviewer boundaries,

104
00:11:52.143 --> 00:11:58.571
expiry conditions, and re-review triggers.
Your evidence is the tuple,

105
00:11:58.571 --> 00:12:05.000
terms matrix, lineage map, gap ledger, and
bounded disposition.

106
00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:10.000
Begin the knowledge check when you can
identify the complete

107
00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:15.000
deployment tuple, limit access claims to
evidence, choose controlling terms,

108
00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:20.000
preserve lineage gaps, route consequential
ambiguity, and recognize re-review

109
00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:25.000
triggers. The check begins only when you
select Begin knowledge

110
00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:30.000
check.

111
00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:35.000
Remember: available is not identified,
identified is not authorized, and

112
00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:40.000
authorized is not proven safe. Preserve
exact artifacts, exact terms,

113
00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:45.000
explicit gaps, distinct reviewer
authority, and a date when the

114
00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:50.000
decision must be examined again.
